WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.679 --> 00:00:09.679
Word up homies!

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:14.740
Welcome back to Thug Notes. This week we settin sail with Moby-Dick by Herman Melville.

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.860
This big ass book starts when some playa
 callin himself Ishmael

00:00:21.860 --> 00:00:25.860
decides he wanna get himself a lil taste
 of life as a whaler.

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.399
But before my boy finds a crew to
join up, he rolls over to the Spouter Inn

00:00:30.399 --> 00:00:34.159
where he hooks up wit some tatted-up
 harpooner named Queequeg.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:38.579
Not long after, they get all tight and start kickin it
Bert and Ernie style.

00:00:38.579 --> 00:00:44.179
So Ishmael and Queequeg fly they colors and crew up on a hoopty-ass boat called the Pequod.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:49.560
After a while the ships top-dog Ahab struts up to the deck with his janky ivory leg

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:55.860
and startin layin down some real talk. He say the Pequod only got one mission: to find Moby Dick, the white whale

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.860
the white whale that took
his leg, and straight OJ that b*tch.

00:00:59.860 --> 00:01:04.680
After about 500 pages of Ishmael
goin off about whaling bullsh*t,

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:10.020
the Pequod cruises up to a ship called the Rachel, where
Ahab starts jabbering with the captain.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:15.200
He ask Ahab if he wanna do em a solid and help search for a lost boat with his son on it.

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:20.880
But Ahab shakes dat load off cuz he only got one thing on his mind: dat Mo-Deezy.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:26.040
Finally they find Moby lurkin in
the water and chase his pasty ass for three days.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:31.320
On the third day, Moby’s fat ass straight rams
the Pequod, which starts sinkin.

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:37.240
Now Ahab ain’t goin out like no b*tch,  so he keeps it clutch and goes toe-to-toe with Moby D.

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:43.820
He whips out his chrome and shanks dat whale, but Moby ain’t playin no mo and drags his ass to the deep.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.960
Woo! You know he dead.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:52.620
In the end, the whole crew go belly-up cept my boy Ishmael, who gets saved by the righteous cats of the Rachel.

00:01:56.560 --> 00:02:01.400
Open up yo eyes and peep this
character foil, son. Unlike Ahab’s crochety ass,

00:02:01.409 --> 00:02:06.389
Ishmael knows how to deal with all the
bunk-ass sh*t the world droppin on him. Check it:

00:02:06.389 --> 00:02:10.389
"Who ain't a slave? ... However they may thump and punch me about...

00:02:10.389 --> 00:02:14.269
everybody else is one way or other served much the same way."

00:02:14.269 --> 00:02:18.820
"Talk not to me of blasphemy, man. I'd strike the sun if it insulted me."

00:02:18.820 --> 00:02:23.800
See, my boy Ishmael ain’t trippin bout the fact that the world’s a twisted place that gonna burn a brotha.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.820
In fact, he totally cool with the fact that ain’t nothing you can do but sit back and accept it.

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:33.520
Whereas Ahab don’t take sh*t from nobody,
even God himself.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:37.180
To Ahab, Big Moby sometimes representing God.

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:41.800
In the game of life, Ahab don’t wanna just
play the hand he was dealt. Naw blood.

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:47.160
He wanna spit in the face of the dealer, cuz ain’t nobody gonna impose rules on Ahab without a fight.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:54.620
So be it the sun, God, or eternity itself, Ahab gonna step up and buck it — even if it kills him.

00:02:54.620 --> 00:02:57.700
So what’s Ahab’s beef with da big G really
all about?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:03.940
To Ahab, God runs every part of this janky-ass world like a tyrant that ain’t got no accountability.

00:03:03.940 --> 00:03:07.260
What’s worse, they always gonna be some simple-ass fools

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:10.840
duped in to thinking that all them injustices ain’t no thang.

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:16.640
Only Ahab sees that God doin em straight dirty.
And even God aint gettin away with punkin Captain A.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:23.140
But since Ahab ain’t got his glock 9 handy, he gotta strap up with a special harpoon to merc this whale.

00:03:23.140 --> 00:03:28.880
Ahab dunks the harpoon in the blood of three pagans, and even BAPTIZES his new piece, saying,

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:33.300
"I do not baptize you in the name of the Father,
but in the name of the Devil."

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:37.300
But other times, that blubbery mess 
reppin all the evil in the world.

00:03:37.300 --> 00:03:39.860
And since evil existin everywhere up in this hood,

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:43.680
some sailors swear they’ve peeped Moby 
in multiple places at once.

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:48.020
And other times Moby Dick is a symbol for an empty, Godless universe.

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:54.320
"To Ishmael, the whale's indefinite whiteness shadows forth the heartless voids and immensities of the universe,

00:03:54.320 --> 00:04:01.880
and thus stabs us from behind with the thought of annihilation. It's a colorless, all-color of atheism from which we shrink.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:05.700
Since whiteness is both the lack of color and the combo of all colors,

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:10.120
that whale is a swimming symbol of the raw truth that,
no matter how you spit it,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:15.020
the sum total of all the things in the 
universe is a big, fat nothing.

00:04:15.020 --> 00:04:19.440
So that whale servin as a nasty reminder that if you gonna live a life seeking meaning,

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:22.920
you best prep yourself for a whole
lot of pain and misery, B.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:28.030
And if you've got the balls to face the universe’s emptiness, you’ll see that we all just like Ishmael —

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:33.930
just a bunch orphans floating aimlessly in a sea
that keeps flowing like it don’t even give a sh*t.

00:04:33.930 --> 00:04:41.320
But keep floating, homies, cuz somewhere out there we all got our own Rachel that's there to save us.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.560
See you next week, B.

